0..76 Comment "// Two rules of a nominal theory that overlap below an abstraction. A rule\'s"
77..153 Comment "// abstraction is one head at any depth, so the checker finds the pair there"
154..184 Comment "// as the kernel does (#1709)."
186..264 Comment "/// `inner` rewrites the restriction inside `nu(bind a . nu(bind b . z()))` to"
265..344 Comment "/// `nu(bind a . w())`, a normal form, while `outer` rewrites the whole term to"
345..424 Comment "/// `z()`. The completion orients the two reducts into a rule of their own, and"
425..465 Comment "/// the kernel replays it from the pair."
